cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata.
title: "sphere-sim: a physically-based simulator of a projected spherical display, with a deliberately independent alignment solver"
abstract: >-
  A forward model of a four-projector Science On a Sphere installation and an
  inverse model that recovers projector pose from photographs, built so that the
  two share no geometry code, no projection math and no distortion model. The
  separation is enforced mechanically by a lint rule in CI rather than by
  convention, because a simulator that shares math with the solver it scores is
  scoring its own assumptions. Every physical constant carries a provenance
  class; geometric parameters are documented or solved for and are optimised
  against, photometric parameters are unmeasured and are therefore built, tested
  and reported as PROVISIONAL rather than tuned.
type: software
authors:
